The [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says of #4471: *known, one issue, one fix queued.* We
ran the desk's own components over the [export](https://github.com/xollaborator/mega.dev) the
desk shipped on 2026-10-04. The ticket holds **two causes**, and intake's tags hid one of
them. This page counts what the ticket actually shows; the numbers are computed from
`reports-4471.json` at render time, not typed.

<SplitSummary ticket={4471} />

## The split

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Both causes put a booking on the wrong day, so the subjects match and [decision
0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges them into one ticket. The merge is cheap;
the cost is the second reading, which nobody did until the components said so.

## Tickets

- **[parser · 379 reports](/kb/incidents/4471)** — the known issue, and #4471 stays its
  ticket. Fix queued.
- **[hint · 33 reports](https://github.com/xollaborator/mega.dev/issues/1)** — `booking-v3`
  prints an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint under the date field; all three tenants on that form write the
  day first. Their people type what the hint says; the form reads it the tenant's way. A
  different bug, a different fix: the parser fix does not touch it.
- **[intake tags · 38 reports](https://github.com/xollaborator/mega.dev/issues/2)** — 23
  `parser` reports tagged `hint`, 15 `hint` reports tagged `parser`. `causes.ts` says the tag
  is a guess; 38 of 412 guesses point the wrong way, and the guess is how one cause stayed
  inside the other's ticket.

<Callout>
Merging by subject is right and stays. But a merged ticket is not one bug. Before you write
"one issue, one fix queued", run the causes, not the subjects.
</Callout>

The desk keeps working while pages are written: counts here are as of the 2026-10-04 export
snapshot. The 5 reports footnoted on the incident page as read as a one-day move all sit in
`parser`; nothing in them changes this split.

## How it landed

The desk's engineering update, 05 October: **#4471 closed.** `parser` — fixed,
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. `hint` — won't fix: the `booking-v3` form was
retired, and the problem goes away with it. 33 reports were carried by a bug the desk never
had to fix, because the desk that retired the form knew what it was retiring. Both tickets in
[xollaborator/mega.dev](https://github.com/xollaborator/mega.dev) closed the same day.

